      "id": "def-relative-compactness-with-respect-to-an-operator",
      "location": "Definition, well-definedness clause 2 (Independence of z)",
      "defect": "false-claim",
      "evidence": "Clause 2 states: \"For z,w in rho(A) the resolvent identity gives BR_A(z) = BR_A(w) + (z-w)BR_A(w)R_A(z)\". With the library convention R_A(z) = (z-A)^{-1} the resolvent identity is R_A(z) - R_A(w) = (w-z)R_A(z)R_A(w), i.e. BR_A(z) = BR_A(w) - (z-w)BR_A(w)R_A(z); the displayed sign is wrong. Counterexample: A = 0 (self-adjoint) and B = I on C, z = 2, w = 3: the left side is 1/2, while the written right side is 1/3 + (2-3)(1/3)(1/2) = 1/6. The independence-of-z conclusion survives with the corrected sign, but the displayed identity is false.",
      "severity": "fatal",
